exports[`meili config sync-with-cloud > prints its help without any network call 1`] = `
"Give every Meilisearch Cloud project of the scope an entry of the config file, with its cloud identifiers, and its master key when the entry has no key. Never replaces a key, never removes an entry. Prints one item per project.

USAGE
  $ meili config sync-with-cloud [-o <mode>] [--debug] [--all] [--team-ids <ids>]
    [--project-name <name>] [--project-url <url>]

FLAGS
  -o, --output=<mode>        json (default): one document, the API body as it
                             is, indented in a terminal, compact when piped.
                             ndjson: one item per line, list commands only,
                             streams with --all.
      --all                  Every project the token sees.
      --debug                Print every HTTP request and response on stderr,
                             secrets redacted.
      --project-name=<name>  The projects with exactly this name, in any team.
      --project-url=<url>    The project with this URL, same scheme and host.
      --team-ids=<ids>       The projects of these teams, comma-separated.

DESCRIPTION
  Give every Meilisearch Cloud project of the scope an entry of the config file,
  with its cloud identifiers, and its master key when the entry has no key.
  Never replaces a key, never removes an entry. Prints one item per project.

  The file holds API keys and decides where every later command goes, for every
  process that reads it: an agent runs this only when the human asked for it
  explicitly.

EXAMPLES
  $ meili config sync-with-cloud --all

  $ meili config sync-with-cloud --team-ids 12,13

  $ meili config sync-with-cloud --project-name prod

  $ meili config sync-with-cloud --project-url https://ms-abc.sfo.meilisearch.io --output json

"
`;
